; 32-syntax.kurt

; `syntax` prints everything Kurt currently knows about a symbol's grammar:
; its fixity (infix/prefix/postfix/bindop), arity, boolean signature,
; aliases, and so on -- the same "syntax info" block `parse` (31-parse.kurt)
; shows, but for one symbol on demand, and without needing an example
; expression to parse first.

bool A
syntax implies

; With no argument, `syntax` prints *all* declared syntax, at every level:
syntax
